.TH wall-c 1 "September 2026" "wall-c 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wall-c \- send Wake-on-LAN magic packets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wall-c
[\-m MAC]
[\-b IP]
[\-\-interface IFACE]
[\-p PORT]
[\-\-count N]
[\-\-interval-ms MS]
[\-\-dry-run]
[\-\-quiet]
[\-\-smart]
[\-y]
[\-h]
[\-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBwall-c\fR sends Wake-on-LAN magic packets over UDP broadcast.
A target MAC is supplied explicitly with \-m/\-\-mac or as one line on stdin.
There is no configuration-file parser or target database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mac MAC
Target MAC address. Accepted forms: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX, XX-XX-XX-XX-XX-XX, XXXXXXXXXXXX.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-broadcast IP
Broadcast IPv4 address (default: 255.255.255.255).
.TP
.B \-\-interface IFACE
Resolve broadcast IPv4 from an interface. Cannot be combined with \-b/\-\-broadcast.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port PORT
UDP destination port (default: 9).
.TP
.B \-\-count N
Number of packets to send (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-\-interval-ms MS
Delay in milliseconds between repeated sends (default: 0).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Validate inputs and print actions without sending.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce non-error output.
.TP
.B \-\-smart
Best-effort pre-send awake check and post-send wake verification.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH TARGET SOURCE
Target selection is:
.IP "1." 3
\-m/\-\-mac
.IP "2." 3
One MAC line from stdin
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success or user cancellation.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, input, interface-resolution, probe/send, or option failure.
